{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Sevenfold</b> — seven specifically, thus: 'את הכבשה ישלם ארבעתים' (he shall pay fourfold for the lamb). Like 'וארבע צאן תחת השה' (and four sheep for the lamb). Similarly: 'שבעתים יוקם קין' (sevenfold shall Cain be avenged). The meaning is like the construct of 'seven days.' And because most payments for theft, when the thief is sold, are five, and when found close to two, therefore he said: sevenfold." "<b>All the wealth of his house he gives</b> — until he pays sevenfold. And HaShem already said: 'ונמכר בגנבתו' (and he shall be sold for his theft). But the adulterer of another man's wife lacks sense, for if a man destroys his own soul, he brings about the destruction, whereas this one — 'הוא יעשנה' (he does it)."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Reading וקרוב as 'and close to' (i.e., approximately two when the stolen item is found intact); the syntax is compressed and the phrase may be elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:18.222975842Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}